+# smallpt / studio
+
+Kevin Beason’s [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) compiled from C++ to WebAssembly. Open `index.html` through your static web host. Generated JavaScript and Wasm are included in `assets/`, so a host needs no compilation step. ES modules and Wasm require HTTP(S), rather than a `file://` page.
+
+The page automatically renders a Cornell box at 720 × 480. Randomize colors changes the two wall colors, back wall, mirror sphere, and glass sphere and restarts rendering. Quality controls samples per pixel; PNG export saves the latest rendered frame. Reset restores the original colors.
+
+## Build
+
+Install Emscripten with `em++` on PATH, then run:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+```
+
+The build compiles `src/renderer.cpp` into `assets/smallpt.js` and `assets/smallpt.wasm`, checks browser JavaScript syntax, and executes the actual Wasm module in Node to check rendering, changed sphere colors, and deterministic reset. No server is started.
+
+The original C++ is retained in `src/smallpt-original.cpp`, with its MIT license in `src/LICENSE.smallpt.txt`. The adaptation retains smallpt’s intersection and radiance calculations, uses progressive 2 × 2 subpixel passes and accumulated radiance, adds a recursion safety limit, and exposes a small C API. It runs exclusively in a dedicated module Web Worker, transfers complete RGBA frames, and yields between row batches so a new render can cancel the previous one. It requires no SharedArrayBuffer or cross-origin isolation headers.
+
+`assets/preview.png` was rendered from the same C++ implementation at 128 samples per pixel; it appears while the first live Wasm pass is computed. Fonts use Google Fonts with local system fallbacks. All tracing runs locally; no rendering service or API key is used.
+
+Browser verification was intentionally skipped; no development or preview server was started.
